  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 4134,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "We recently made a change to how report invitations in order to make the [Disclosure Assistance](https://support.hackerone.com/hc/en-us/articles/115001936043) process better. Parts of this change regressed the fix we made in #123420 regarding how report invitations (such as to become an external participant) are handled. @japzdivino notified of this regression and worked with us to get the logic back to the previous intent.\n\nTo correct this issue, we added logic that ties report invitation links to a user if the user exists on the platform (either the username or the e-mail address). If the invitation link was sent to an e-mail address not matching an existing user on HackerOne, any user can still consume the invitation.\n\nWe are disclosing this report under Limited Visibility due to multiple attachments and comments including e-mail addresses, as this was part of the POC.",
